{
 "concept": "Red-brick Victorian factory complex. Landmark is a tall clock tower (octagon, 8x8 footprint, 4 floors plus a spire) that is well over 1.8x the height of the main hall. A wide sawtooth-roofed machine hall (25x17, 11 high) forms the body, with a lower two-storey workshop wing attached beside it and a small boiler house set back as a step-down. Materials: red bricks on both pillar and wall2 for the main colour, polished deepslate base, cut copper trim, with copper-oxidised roof accents. Features: two brick smokestacks and a chimney on the boiler house, a pipe rack on the hall's south face, a gear on the workshop wall, a clock on the tower, a porch at the main entrance, and a bridge across the yard gap to the boiler house. All detail is outside so the interiors stay big.",
